  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Basic Needs and Essential Services for IDPs, Returnees and other War-Affected Ukrainians</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	Provision of protection activities
UNHCR&#x2019;s protection response under the proposed project will be structured around a three-pronged approach combining direct service provision, state system strengthening, and community-based protection mechanisms, aligned with Ukraine&#x2019;s social protection reform agenda and UNHCR&#x2019;s 2025 Protection Strategy.             
I.	Direct Service Provision
UNHCR will directly provide critical legal assistance, including primary and secondary legal aid and representative. UNHCR legal programme will place a particular focus on people with disabilities, older persons, and other people with specific needs in areas impacted by ongoing war.                                                       II.	State System Strengthening
UNHCR will support the Government of Ukraine, particularly the Ministry of Social Policy (MoSP), in strengthening national protection and social service systems to enhance their responsiveness, inclusivity, and sustainability, especially in light of the needs of older people, persons with disabilities, and displaced populations                  
III.	Community-Based Protection Systems
Recognizing the central role of communities in protection, UNHCR will continue to reinforce and scale up its support to local protection systems, ensuring that community-level initiatives are integrated into broader state systems.
2)	Provision of cash assistance: 
I.	Provision of Cash for Winter Energy Needs                                                        
II.	Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA), including Emergency MPCA                  3)	Shelter support in collective sites</narrative>
  </description>
